{
  "id": "COMPOUND:19464 - PROTEIN:5788",
  "verbalization": "Dorsmanin D is implicated in the targeting of multiple enzymes in the biosynthetic pathway leading to SNB-78. The evidence suggests that Dorsmanin D acts as a target for two distinct enzymes: Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like and Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. Both of these enzymes are involved in the metabolic pathway that ultimately leads to SNB-78. The shared involvement of these enzymes in the same metabolic route, coupled with the direct targeting of SNB-78 by both, implies a potential mechanism of action where Dorsmanin D modulates the activity of these enzymes, thereby influencing the production of SNB-78. The presence of multiple intermediate metabolites in the pathway further supports the idea that Dorsmanin D may act as a regulator of this biosynthetic process. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the metabolic interactions and underscores the role of Dorsmanin D in modulating the production of SNB-78 through a series of enzymatic steps.",
